{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["And Moshe said to HaShem: The people will not be able, etc. — the commentator who explains that Moshe said thus: 'You already told us this three days ago and you bounded the mountain — השמרו לכם עלות בהר — so why do you need to say it to me now a second time?' — he has made an error. For a person is urged at the time of action even after he was urged before the action; one urges a person a second time at the time of action, to say: now the time has come to do what I said. And furthermore, the second verse that He repeated — He said to him: Go, descend. What does this come to add? Rather, this is what Moshe said to the Holy One, blessed be He, by way of question, and thus he asked Him: Yesterday and the day before you told me that the people would not be able to ascend Mount Sinai, when you warned the people through me with the bounding. You said to me: השמרו לכם עלות בהר. And now you say to me: פן יהרסו אל HaShem — perhaps you are adding that even to come close a little in order to look and see, even far from the mountain, is forbidden?! And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him: Go, descend, and you shall come up, and Aharon with you, and the priests, and the people — let them not break through to ascend to HaShem. And also now, to look without ascending, I did not tell you."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:11.630705440Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}